[32m+[m[32m### Findings requiring follow-up[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Missing migration lock:** `prisma/migrations/migration_lock.toml` is absent.[m
[32m+[m[32m   The schema provider is PostgreSQL. Restore the provider lock in a separately[m
[32m+[m[32m   reviewed change; do not invent database migration checksums. Prisma expects[m
[32m+[m[32m   the migration directory, including the provider lock, to be versioned.[m
[32m+[m[32m   [Prisma migration histories](https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/v7/prisma-migrate/understanding-prisma-migrate/migration-histories).[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Nullable-array CHECK gaps:** commerce `features TEXT[]` and portal[m
[32m+[m[32m   enrollment/guardian `scopes TEXT[]` permit SQL NULL. Their cardinality-based[m
[32m+[m[32m   CHECKs can consequently accept invalid rows when the other required terms[m
[32m+[m[32m   are satisfied. PostgreSQL accepts a CHECK whose expression is NULL, not only[m
[32m+[m[32m   true. This is a statically established integrity gap, not an executed SQL[m
[32m+[m[32m   reproduction or a demonstrated API privilege escalation. Application input[m
[32m+[m[32m   validation does not substitute for the database invariant.[m
[32m+[m[32m   [PostgreSQL CHECK semantics](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/ddl-constraints.html).[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Subject-code upgrade collisions:** `UPPER(REPLACE(slug, '-', '_'))` can map[m
[32m+[m[32m   distinct slugs such as `a-b` and `a_b`, or case variants, to the same code[m
[32m+[m[32m   before creation of a unique index. Existing-data collisions were not queried.[m
[32m+[m[32m   Empty-database replay alone cannot verify this populated-upgrade behavior.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Guardian consent enforcement uses a `NOT VALID` constraint, leaving legacy[m
[32m+[m[32m   rows unvalidated. Application access fails closed, but existing rows need an[m
[32m+[m[32m   approved review before constraint validation; never manufacture consent.[m
[32m+[m[32m   Legacy memberships require explicit verification rather than automatic trust.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Enum alterations require a compatible PostgreSQL version; the future[m
[32m+[m[32m   disposable setup below targets PostgreSQL 17. Chronological dependencies look[m
[32m+[m[32m   consistent statically, but server parsing and transactional compatibility[m
[32m+[m[32m   remain unverified.[m
